description:
Implement a module that sorts two input values and outputs them in descending order. The module takes two 8-bit wide inputs and produces two outputs: the first output will hold the larger value, while the second output will contain the smaller value, effectively providing a simple sorting mechanism for the two input data words.
module top_module(
	dataIn0, dataIn1,
	dataOut0, dataOut1
);

code:
module top_module(
	dataIn0, dataIn1,
	dataOut0, dataOut1
);parameter DATA_SIZE = 8;	 

input 		[DATA_SIZE - 1:0] dataIn0;
input 		[DATA_SIZE - 1:0] dataIn1;
output reg 	[DATA_SIZE - 1:0] dataOut0;
output reg 	[DATA_SIZE - 1:0] dataOut1;



always @(*) begin


	if(dataIn0 > dataIn1) begin
		dataOut0 = dataIn0;
		dataOut1 = dataIn1;
	end else begin
		dataOut0 = dataIn1;
		dataOut1 = dataIn0;
	end
end

endmodule

