description:
Design a 4-bit binary adder that calculates the sum of two 4-bit inputs, A and B. The output, SUM, is generated using combinational logic to handle each bit's addition, incorporating XOR operations for bit addition and AND/OR gates to manage carry propagation across the bits. Each bit of the SUM output is computed considering the previous bits' carry effect, allowing for accurate addition of the two 4-bit numbers.
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [3:0] SUM
);

code:
module top_module(
    input [3:0] A,
    input [3:0] B,
    output reg [3:0] SUM
);always @* begin
        SUM[0] = A[0] ^ B[0];
        SUM[1] = (A[1] ^ B[1]) ^ (A[0] & B[0]);
        SUM[2] = (A[2] ^ B[2]) ^ ((A[1] & B[1]) | (A[0] & B[0]));
        SUM[3] = (A[3] ^ B[3]) ^ ((A[2] & B[2]) | (A[1] & B[1]) | (A[0] & B[0]));
    end

endmodule

