description:
Design a sequence detector that identifies a specific pattern of input bits. The circuit transitions through three states: S0, S1, and S2. It detects the transition from '1' to '0' (input = 1 followed by input = 0) and then back to '1' (input = 0 followed by input = 1). When the entire sequence of '1' followed by '0' and then '1' is detected, the output signal is set high. Otherwise, it remains low. The module uses a synchronous state machine to control state transitions based on the input signal.
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);

code:
module top_module(
  input in,
  output out
);// Define the states of the state machine
  parameter S0 = 2'b00;
  parameter S1 = 2'b01;
  parameter S2 = 2'b10;

  // Define the current state variable
  reg [1:0] state;

  // Define the output signal
  reg out_reg;

  // Implement the state machine using a case statement
  always @(posedge in) begin
    case (state)
      S0: begin
        if (in == 1'b1) begin
          state <= S1;
        end else begin
          state <= S0;
        end
      end
      S1: begin
        if (in == 1'b0) begin
          state <= S2;
        end else begin
          state <= S0;
        end
      end
      S2: begin
        if (in == 1'b1) begin
          state <= S0;
          out_reg <= 1'b1;
        end else begin
          state <= S0;
        end
      end
    endcase
  end

  // Assign the output signal
  assign out = out_reg;

endmodule

