description:
Design a pipelined XOR gate that takes two binary inputs, `a` and `b`, and produces a single output `out_comb`. The output is computed through two stages of registers, where the result of the XOR operation is stored in intermediate registers before being provided as output. This design effectively introduces two clock cycles of latency for the output to be available after the inputs are applied, enhancing the throughput for cascaded operations in a larger digital system.
module top_module(
    input a,
    input b,
    output reg out_comb
);

code:
module top_module(
    input a,
    input b,
    output reg out_comb
);reg [1:0] stage1;
    reg [1:0] stage2;

    always @ (a, b) begin
        stage1[0] <= a ^ b;
        stage1[1] <= stage1[0];
        stage2[0] <= stage1[1];
        stage2[1] <= stage2[0];
        out_comb <= stage2[1];
    end

endmodule

