Design a finite state machine (FSM) that transitions between four defined states based on a 4-bit input signal. The states are represented using two different encoding schemes: binary and one-hot. The module takes an input to determine the next state from the current state and outputs a corresponding 2-bit signal that varies based on the current state and the chosen encoding format. The FSM utilizes combinational logic for state transition definitions and sequential logic for state storage, which updates on the rising edge of the clock signal.
